    "subject": "biochemistry",
    "originalNumber": 6,
    "stem": "A 9-year old girl is brought to her physician for an assessment of potential causes for her increased vision problems. Examination demonstrates that her eye movement is impaired and she has pigmentary retinopathy. Her physician suspects the child has Kearns-Sayre syndrome which is caused by a defect in complex II of the electron transport chain. If this diagnosis is correct, oxidation of which of the following substrates would be associated with impaired electron transfer?",
