    "id": "notion-biochemistry-0035",
    "subject": "biochemistry",
    "originalNumber": 35,
    "stem": "Which of the following factors in present only in the intrinsic pathway of blood coagulation?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Factor II"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Factor X"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Factor I"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Factor VIII"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "The intrinsic pathway responds to spontaneous, internal damage of the vascular endothelium whereas the extrinsic pathway becomes activated secondary to external trauma. Both intrinsic and extrinsic pathways meet at a shared point to continue coagulation, the common pathway.\nClotting factors involved in the intrinsic pathway include Factors XII, XI, IX, and VIII.\nClotting factors involved in the extrinsic pathway include Factors VII and III.\nThe common pathway includes clotting factors X, V, II, I, and XIII.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Factor II, or Prothrombin, is part of the common pathway of blood coagulation.\nIt is activated to thrombin in the final steps of the coagulation cascade.",
      "B": "Factor X is a part of both the intrinsic and extrinsic pathways.\nIt serves as a link between the intrinsic and extrinsic pathways, as it is activated in the common pathway.",
      "C": "Factor I, or Fibrinogen, is part of the common pathway.\nIt is converted to fibrin by thrombin in the final stages of blood clotting.",
      "D": "The intrinsic pathway responds to spontaneous, internal damage of the vascular endothelium whereas the extrinsic pathway becomes activated secondary to external trauma. Both intrinsic and extrinsic pathways meet at a shared point to continue coagulation, the common pathway.\nClotting factors involved in the intrinsic pathway include Factors XII, XI, IX, and VIII.\nClotting factors involved in the extrinsic pathway include Factors VII and III.\nThe common pathway includes clotting factors X, V, II, I, and XIII."
    },
