    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Peroxidase is an enzyme that catalyzes the reaction ⁍.\nThis reaction involves the conversion of Fe2+ (ferrous ion) to Fe3+ (ferric ion) and the reduction of molecular oxygen (O) to water (HO). The peroxidase enzyme facilitates this reaction by providing a suitable environment for the transfer of electrons and the formation of the products. It acts as a catalyst, speeding up the reaction without being consumed in the process. Therefore, peroxidase is the enzyme that catalyzes this specific reaction.",
