    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "SIMILAR TO BOARD EXAM CONCEPT. Lactase\nintolerence is caused by a deficiency of lactase (a\ndisaccharidase) in the intestinal brush border. Lactose\nis unable to be broken down into glucose and\ngalactose, and thus accumulates in the gut. It is\neventually fermented by bacteria to form hydrogen,\nmethane and carbon dioxide, leading to various\nabdominal symptoms. 3 questions pertaining to\nlactase deficiency were asked during our\nBiochemistry exam",
