    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Decreases Vmax and increases Km."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Decreases Vmax and has no effect on Km."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Has no effect on Vmax or Km."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Has no effect on Vmax and increases Km."
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "NOTA"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "A noncompetitive inhibitor binds to the enzyme at a\nsite other than\nthe substrate binding site, so it has little measurable\neffect on the enzyme’s affinity for substrate, as\nrepresented by the Km. However, the inhibitor has the\neffect of decreasing\nthe availability of active enzyme capable of catalyzing\nthe reaction, which manifests itself as a decrease in\nVmax.",
