    "explanation": "Fructose intolerance is an autosomal recessive\ndisorder resulting from deficiency in Aldolase B.\nPatient present wirh hypoglycemia, jaundice, cirrhosis\nand vvomiting due to accumulation of fructose 1-P\nphosphate. (Decrease glycogenolysis, and decrease\ngluconeogenesis). In Essential fructosuria, there is a\ndefect in fructokinase. However, it is more benign and\nasymptomatic. Galactokinase deficiency presents with\ngalactosuria and cataracts in early childhood. Classic\ngalactosemia may present with vomiting, diarrhea\nafter milk ingestion (not after ingestion of fruit juice).",
