    "explanation": "SIMILAR TO PREVIOUS BOARD EXAM\nCONCEPT/PRINCIPLE. Bohr effect is dependent\ncooperative interaction between hemes of more than\none domain.this is only represented in hemoglobin\nwhich has a tetrameric structure. Letter A is correct\nsince myoglobin contains a heme protein. B- is also\ncorrect, since the only major difference between\nhemoglobin and myoglobin is that the latter has only\ndomain while the former exhibits 4 domains. their\nalpha helix and tertiary configuration is very similar.\nboth myoglobin and hemoglobin needs a reduced\nstate of iron (ferrous form) to allow binding of oxygen\nfor storage or for transport.",
