    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Competitive inhibition is best extrapolated using line\nweaver burk plot since it can easily demonstrate the\nvalues of Km and Vmax. It is also called as substrate\nanalog they bind to the catalytic site decreasing the\nnumber of free enzyme molecules availabe for\nsubstrate binding. kinetics will show that affinity will\nbe decreased as manifested by increase in Km ( note\nthat Km and affinity has inverse relationship) and\nwith no effect to the Vmax regardless of the amount of\nthe inhibitor",
