    "explanation": "Vitamin K, a fat soluble vitamin, is an essential\ncofactor for the synthesis of factors II, VII, IX and X. It\nDECREASES/SHORTENS the coagulation time\n(particularly the PT). It is synthesized by the normal\ngut flora and is present at low concentration in\ncow's/breast milk.",
