    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "this is a classic case of Pompe disease caused by\ndeficiency of a 1,4 glucosidase aka acid maltase. It is a\nform of enzyme defect wherein there is accumulation\nof glycogen granules inside the lysosomes. It doesn’t\npresent with hypoglycemia and lactic acidosis since\nenzymes for glycogen metabolism are intact. the most\ncommon presentation is cardiomyopathy with heart\nfailure. no treatment is available and death usually\noccurs at 1 mo of age. Devlin p 621.",
