    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "CPS I absolutely requires N-acetyl glutamate as an\nallosteric activator. In the urea cycle, 3 molecules of\nATP are required but ultimately 4 ATP equivalents are\nconsumed, (2 ATP for CPS I and 1 ATP for\nargininosuccinate synthetase [converted to AMP\nhence 2 equivalents used]). The cycle can also be used\nto synthesize ornithine, citrulline, arginine, fumarate\nand urea. Lippincott 5th pg 254",
