    "id": "superexam-biochemistry-0539",
    "subject": "biochemistry",
    "originalNumber": 539,
    "stem": "A 4-month-old boy is being evaluated for seizures,\npsychomotor retardation, and hypotonia. Work-up\nreveals elevated serum levels of lactate alanine,\npyruvate, and ketoacids. Based on the clinical\npresentation, pyruvate carboxylase activity is measured\nusing fibroblasts from a skin biopsy and is found to be\nmarkedly decreased. This enzyme is normally used to\ndirectly synthesize which of the following molecules?",
