    "id": "superexam-biochemistry-0596",
    "subject": "biochemistry",
    "originalNumber": 596,
    "stem": "An athlete who has extensive training of 8 hours per day\nhas a higher energy requirement than people who have\nsedentary lifestyles. Most of the energy requirement is\nused for?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Metabolism in skeletal muscles during physical\nactivity for rapid and sustain effort"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Metabolism in cardiac and respiratory cells to\nmaintain adequate oxygen and nutrient delivery to all\ncells of the body"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Metabolism in nerve cells needed to conduct\nelectrical impulses and control bodily functions"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Metabolism in the GIT to extract nutrients needed to\nsustain the energy requirements"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Metabolism in cells to maintain homeostasis such as\nthe maintenance of the Na/K pump"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "No matter the physical activity, the basal metabolic\nrate accounts for at least 50% of energy requirements.\nMost of the basal metabolic rate is used for the\nmaintenance of cellular functions such as the\nmaintenace of the cellular electrolyte composition by\nthe Na/K pump.",
