    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Promoter regions are part of the DNA where RNA\npolymerase binds to start transcription. The primary\ntranscript is a linear copy of the transcriptional unit,\nthe segment of DNA between specific initiation and\ntermination sequences. Rho factor is involved in\ntermination of DNA transcription by binding to a C-\nrich region near the 3'-end of the newly synthesized\nRNA and migrates along the 5' to 3' direction until\ntermination site is reached.",
